                    insight_upheld:         `Order upheld: you tested the market rather than accepting it, used the HHI screen as a trigger, produced a price-effect estimate inside the evidenced band, disciplined the synergies, and cured the harm with a proportionate structural divestiture. The order protects shoppers, survives the NCLAT, and lets the benign part of the deal proceed.`,
                    insight_overturned:     `Overturned: the order rests on assumption rather than tested evidence, or on a recommendation the findings don't support. Either the market was never SSNIP-tested, the price effect was never estimated, or the remedy was disproportionate — and that is exactly the seam an appeal exploits.`,
                    insight_mixed:          `A contested result: the analysis is partly sound but the chain from market definition to estimate to order has gaps. It may survive, but the parties' economists will press every assumption you didn't anchor in the data.`,
                    insight_untested:       `You never ran the SSNIP / hypothetical-monopolist test on a narrow market — so every share, HHI and effect downstream was measured on a market boundary you assumed rather than proved. Market definition is the foundation; build it on evidence.`,
                    insight_typeii:         `You cleared a merger your own estimate says raises prices 6–11% on a staple — a Type II error. Clearing an anticompetitive merger lets prices rise on a product hundreds of millions buy; it is the costliest error precisely because it is the quietest.`,
                    insight_typei:          `You prohibited the entire deal. If the harm was confined to one segment and three states, a targeted divestiture would have cured it — blocking destroys ₹900 crore of claimed synergies and risks a successful appeal that reverses you on proportionality.`,
                    insight_remedy:         `You reached for a remedy rather than a blunt clear-or-block. The quality of a conditional clearance is in the design: a structural divestiture to a credible buyer restores competition cleanly, where a behavioural price cap leaves the Commission policing the market for years.`,
                    insight_clock:          `You ran past the 210-working-day statutory limit. An estimate you can defend on time beats a perfect model delivered late — the parties' financing lapses and the order is vulnerable purely on procedure.`,

                    hint_untested:          `Your downstream HHI and effects rest on a market you never tested. The SSNIP / hypothetical-monopolist test on a narrow market is the foundation — without it the appellate body discounts everything that follows.`,
